Create a complete beginner-friendly web game called **"Dough-Cat"**, a cute bakery shop simulation game.

Use only:

* HTML
* CSS
* Vanilla JavaScript

Do not use React, Node.js, TypeScript, Bootstrap, Tailwind, or other frameworks.

## PROJECT STRUCTURE

Create these files:

```text
Dough-Cat/
├── index.html
├── ingredients.html
├── style.css
└── script.js
```

## 1. BAKERY PAGE - index.html

This is the main bakery page.

Show:

* 🐱 Dough-Cat Bakery title
* 💰 Coins
* 📦 Current ingredient inventory
* 🍩 Donut stock
* 🍞 Bread stock

Starting values:

* Coins: 100
* Flour: 5
* Eggs: 3
* Sugar: 5
* Donuts: 0
* Bread: 0

Add these recipes:

### Donut

Requires:

* 1 Flour
* 1 Egg
* 1 Sugar

When the player clicks "Make Donut":

* Remove the required ingredients
* Add 1 Donut
* Show a message saying the donut was made
* If ingredients are insufficient, show an error message

### Bread

Requires:

* 2 Flour
* 1 Egg

When the player clicks "Make Bread":

* Remove the required ingredients
* Add 1 Bread
* Show a message
* If ingredients are insufficient, show an error message

Add selling buttons:

* Sell Donut → +15 coins
* Sell Bread → +12 coins

If the player has no food to sell, show an error message.

Add a button:

**🛒 Ingredient Shop**

Clicking it must open:

```text
ingredients.html
```

